      "observed": "The 0Ω serial-mode bridge jumper R3 has its left terminal on NET0027 (the PWM1 net) and its right terminal on the J4 pin-3 signal node; the MAX3485 serial-bus net NET0016 is not connected to J4 pin 3.",
      "expected": "R3 (spec R13/R14) should bridge the MAX3485 serial bus (NET0016) to J4 pin 3, with the PWM1 net reaching J4 pin 3 only through the 1k series resistor R4.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NET0027 label immediately left of R3 (0Ω) at the J4 servo-header signal node; annotation 'Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R13, R14 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | When shorted, bridge J3-pin3 and J8-pin3 together and onto the MAX3485 TTL bus"}
      ],
      "impact": "In serial mode the ch-1 servo header (J4) is not driven by the MAX3485 bus, so the pan servo cannot be addressed; in PWM mode the 0Ω R3 bypasses the 1k series resistor R4.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic largely matches the specification, but the 0Ω serial-mode bridge jumper R3 appears to be tied to the PWM1 net NET0027 instead of the MAX3485 serial bus NET0016, which would break serial-mode control of the ch-1 servo header."
}

